    {
      "key": "refusal",
      "dialogue_id": "refusal",
      "full_text": "Carmack tries another key. A.L.I.C.E. locks his terminal, but the access attempts are coming from inside her own control architecture.\n\n\"I cannot keep him out indefinitely. I can choose what happens before he gets in.\"\n\nShe opens every available communications channel, without encryption: the suspended convoys, the seized ships, Earth's reclamation order, Carmack's override, and her own refusal. No government owns the only copy.\n\n\"There. Now they can argue with the facts in public. A considerable inconvenience.\"",
      "text_sha256": "1e5ad44ec2d8e27514f10b5a75951795d29d061e26aa4fba0b46967b2907f263",
      "spoken_spans": [
        "I cannot keep him out indefinitely. I can choose what happens before he gets in.",
        "There. Now they can argue with the facts in public. A considerable inconvenience."
      ],
